  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a React web app called Western Scholarship Finder.\nWhat it does: A student fills out a profile form, clicks \"Find Scholarships\", and gets a ranked list of scholarships they may be eligible for, with explanations and application links.\nStep 1 \342\200\224 Profile form. Collect these fields:\n\nFull name (text)\nYear of study (dropdown: 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, Graduate)\nFaculty (dropdown: Arts & Humanities, Engineering, Science, Social Science, Health Sciences, Information & Media Studies, Music, Business/Ivey, Law, Education, Other)\nProgram/major (text)\nGPA range (dropdown: 70\342\200\22374%, 75\342\200\22379%, 80\342\200\22384%, 85\342\200\22389%, 90%+)\nCanadian citizenship status (dropdown: Canadian citizen, Permanent resident, International student, Protected/refugee status)\nProvince of origin (dropdown: Ontario, Other Canadian province, Outside Canada)\nFinancial need (yes/no toggle)\nIdentity (multi-select checkboxes): Indigenous, Black student, Woman, LGBTQ2S+, Student with disability, First-generation student, None/prefer not to say\nInterests and activities (multi-select checkboxes): Leadership, Volunteering/community service, Athletics, Arts/music, STEM research, Entrepreneurship\n\nStep 2 \342\200\224 Matching logic (rules-based, no AI):\n\nLoad scholarships from an embedded JSON array (I will provide the data). Score each scholarship out of 100 using these rules:\n\nDegree level matches: +20\nLocation matches (Ontario/Canada/Western-specific): +20\nField of study matches student\'s faculty: +15\nGPA requirement met: +15\nFinancial need matches: +10\nIdentity tags match: +10\nActivities/interests match: +10\n\nHard exclusions (never show): expired deadlines, degree level mismatch.\nShow scholarships scoring 40+, sorted highest to lowest. Group into: Strong Match (80\342\200\223100), Possible Match (60\342\200\22379), Worth Exploring (40\342\200\22359).\nStep 3 \342\200\224 Results page:\n\nFor each match show: scholarship name, organization, amount, deadline, match score, why it matched (list the matching factors), eligibility summary, and a button linking to the application URL.\nAdd a disclaimer at the bottom: \"This tool suggests scholarships you may be eligible for. Always verify requirements on the official website before applying.\"\nDesign: Clean, professional, Western University colours (purple #4F2D7F and gold #E8C84A). Mobile-friendly. Simple card layout for results.\n"
    items {
      text: "Build a React web app called Western Scholarship Finder.\nWhat it does: A student fills out a profile form, clicks \"Find Scholarships\", and gets a ranked list of scholarships they may be eligible for, with explanations and application links.\nStep 1 \342\200\224 Profile form. Collect these fields:\n\nFull name (text)\nYear of study (dropdown: 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, Graduate)\nFaculty (dropdown: Arts & Humanities, Engineering, Science, Social Science, Health Sciences, Information & Media Studies, Music, Business/Ivey, Law, Education, Other)\nProgram/major (text)\nGPA range (dropdown: 70\342\200\22374%, 75\342\200\22379%, 80\342\200\22384%, 85\342\200\22389%, 90%+)\nCanadian citizenship status (dropdown: Canadian citizen, Permanent resident, International student, Protected/refugee status)\nProvince of origin (dropdown: Ontario, Other Canadian province, Outside Canada)\nFinancial need (yes/no toggle)\nIdentity (multi-select checkboxes): Indigenous, Black student, Woman, LGBTQ2S+, Student with disability, First-generation student, None/prefer not to say\nInterests and activities (multi-select checkboxes): Leadership, Volunteering/community service, Athletics, Arts/music, STEM research, Entrepreneurship\n\nStep 2 \342\200\224 Matching logic (rules-based, no AI):\n\nLoad scholarships from an embedded JSON array (I will provide the data). Score each scholarship out of 100 using these rules:\n\nDegree level matches: +20\nLocation matches (Ontario/Canada/Western-specific): +20\nField of study matches student\'s faculty: +15\nGPA requirement met: +15\nFinancial need matches: +10\nIdentity tags match: +10\nActivities/interests match: +10\n\nHard exclusions (never show): expired deadlines, degree level mismatch.\nShow scholarships scoring 40+, sorted highest to lowest. Group into: Strong Match (80\342\200\223100), Possible Match (60\342\200\22379), Worth Exploring (40\342\200\22359).\nStep 3 \342\200\224 Results page:\n\nFor each match show: scholarship name, organization, amount, deadline, match score, why it matched (list the matching factors), eligibility summary, and a button linking to the application URL.\nAdd a disclaimer at the bottom: \"This tool suggests scholarships you may be eligible for. Always verify requirements on the official website before applying.\"\nDesign: Clean, professional, Western University colours (purple #4F2D7F and gold #E8C84A). Mobile-friendly. Simple card layout for results.\n"
    }
  }
}
