  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating the Metadata**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a handle on the project\'s core identity. My immediate focus is on updating the `metadata.json` file. It\'s the first step to establish the \"Western Scholarship Finder\" web app properly. I see this as the foundation, which I\'m tackling with precision.\n\n\n**Defining the Form Fields**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in Step 1, the profile form design. I\'ve defined the key fields to collect user data: name, year, faculty, program, GPA, citizenship, province, financial need, and identity/interests using a mix of text inputs, dropdowns, toggles, and multi-select checkboxes, as listed. I believe these are the right fields to collect for matching users and scholarships.\n\n\n**Developing the Matching Logic**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the matching logic, specifically step two. I\'m focusing on a rules-based system, no AI at this stage. I\'m loading scholarships from a JSON array, representing realistic examples. The scoring is designed around factors like degree level, location, field of study, GPA, financial need, identity tags, and activities/interests. I\'m also planning to implement hard exclusions, primarily for expired deadlines.\n\n\n**Refining the Exclusion Criteria**\n\nI\'m now refining the matching rules, concentrating on exclusions. I\'ll include a couple of clearly expired scholarships in the JSON data and filter them out using a `isExpired` flag. The degree level logic is also refined. I also have an improved plan for the results page, including match score breakdowns and an application URL button for each scholarship. Finally, I\'ve defined score groups: Strong, Possible, and Worth Exploring, depending on a score of 40+.\n\n\n**Performing a Skill Check**\n\nI\'ve just completed a skill check to verify requirements for the project\'s simple design. It seems the list of available skills aren\'t relevant to the core, client-side, rule-based approach I\'m implementing. I\'m focusing on the embedded JSON array and client-side logic as the key elements. The design will be clean, professional, and mobile-friendly, using Western University\'s colours, and I\'ll include a simple card layout for the results.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 259091574
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
