  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing the Matcher**\n\nI\'m making excellent progress on `/src/utils/matcher.ts`. This module will implement the scoring and exclusion logic. I\'ve re-examined the user\'s rules: a degree level match is worth +20, as is a location match for Ontario/Canada/Western-specific. Field of study matches also score points.\n\n\n**Refining the Scoring Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the finer details of the scoring rules. I\'m assigning +15 points for faculty and GPA requirement matches, and +10 for financial need, identity tags, and activities/interests alignment. I\'m focusing particularly on the edge cases for degree-level and location matches, with hard exclusions for mismatches.\n\n\n**Consolidating Location Logic**\n\nI\'m simplifying the location matching. A new rule combines province and citizenship: If a student\'s province or citizenship aligns with the scholarship\'s targets, they score +20. This streamlines the logic and addresses potential international student scenarios within province matching. Otherwise, it is a zero score. This is a very robust check I am applying.\n\n\n**Clarifying Match Criteria**\n\nI\'m solidifying the province/citizenship matching logic for location-based criteria. My latest update prioritizes a clean +20 score if both province and citizenship align, or if either is universally open (\"All\"). For partial matches, they earn a +10, and otherwise it is a 0 score. I\'m also now factoring faculty alignment into the scoring, awarding +15 points for matched faculties.\n\n\n**Defining Final Match Rules**\n\nI\'ve finalized the matching rules for faculty, GPA, financial need, and identity tags. Faculty matching now awards +15 if the student\'s faculty is present in the scholarship\'s targets, or if the scholarship targets \"All.\" GPA matching is determined by comparing GPA range ranks, awarding +15 if the student\'s range meets the scholarship\'s minimum. Financial need grants +10 if the scholarship doesn\'t require it, or if the requirement is met. Finally, identity tags award +10 if the scholarship has no specific tags or if the student\'s tags align. I am confident in these final details.\n\n\n**Defining Activity Alignment**\n\nI\'ve streamlined the activity/interest matching. Scholarships with no specific target interests grant a +10 to all students, simplifying the logic. Conversely, if specific interests are targeted, a +10 is awarded only if a student\'s interests include at least one of the scholarship\'s. I\'m satisfied with this logic. I also decided to double check the hard exclusions again to make sure everything is in place!\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 18
      nanos: 186924654
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
