    thinking: "**Adjusting Column Layout**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the responsive layout, specifically the column spans. I\'m adjusting the sidebar to `lg:col-span-4` and the main cards to `lg:col-span-8`. Next, I\'ll design the \"Your Profile Summary Card\" to align with the sidebar\'s design specifications in the HTML.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Summary**\n\nI\'ve integrated the exact code for the profile summary card within the sidebar column. This includes the styling and structure, ensuring it aligns with the design specifications. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, so the card elements adapt correctly to different screen sizes, especially the \"Your Profile\" summary card.\n\n\n**Detailing Profile Summary**\n\nI\'m now detailing the profile summary section. I\'ve focused on displaying the user\'s full name with bold styling and ensured appropriate text size. I\'ve also added the \"Year & Faculty\" and \"Program\" sections, using labels, and formatted the year and faculty data with pills and small font for clarity.\n\n\n**Elaborating Academic Status**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the academic status section of the profile. I\'ve integrated a GPA display with the range, using bold styling for the GPA. I\'m also adding an eligibility status, which is color-coded based on GPA range, making it visually clear. The text for the status will update with the given condition.\n\n\n**Adding Background Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Background & Attributes\" section into the profile. I\'ve included the financial need indicator, highlighting it with an amber-colored tag. The identities and interests are displayed as tags, using a consistent style for each. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements are visually distinct and easy to understand.\n\n\n**Integrating Edit Profile**\n\nI\'ve integrated the edit profile button and ensured it\'s functional, using the `handleReset` functionality. I\'ve styled it with a distinct appearance for easy identification. The button\'s placement is now correctly handled, with proper spacing and visual separation, including hover and active states. I am refining the visual presentation for user clarity.\n\n\n**Implementing Match Filters**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Refine Matches\" section into the interface. I\'ve started by adding a header and category tabs for filtering. I am now working on the individual filter options. The filter options are all being populated dynamically based on data, and the count per category is being updated correctly.\n\n\n**Refining Match Filters**\n\nI\'m now refining the match filter tabs for a seamless user experience. I\'m focusing on the \"Worth Exploring\" tab and ensuring the tab labels accurately reflect the filter counts. I\'m dynamically updating the filter options based on the available data to ensure the counts are current, while emphasizing visual clarity. I\'m now testing the responsiveness.\n\n\n**Adding Sort Options**\n\nI\'ve integrated a sort dropdown for match results. It\'s fully functional now, with options for match score, award amount (descending), and deadline (alphabetical). I\'ve focused on styling it consistently with the interface and added an optional faculty sub-filter. I\'m prioritizing user control and clear presentation.\n\n\n**Adding Faculty Filter**\n\nI\'ve integrated a faculty exclusivity filter within the sorting options. I\'ve included a select dropdown that lists various faculties. The options update correctly and include appropriate styling to maintain consistency. This allows users to narrow their match search based on faculty. I\'m prioritizing user control and clear presentation.\n\n\n"
