  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Scholarship IDs**\n\nI\'ve got it! The scholarship list looks great, with those distinctive IDs like `w-presidents-entrance`. I am going to focus on how this information matches the data the user provided.\n\n\n**Considering Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s data; it\'s a JSON list of 52 scholarships. I\'m trying to determine the best strategy for integrating this into the application. My initial thought is to update the core scholarship data. Should I combine the lists or replace the existing one? It seems the user wants this dataset used in real-time, matching and searching the new real scholarships. I\'ll need to figure out the best approach.\n\n\n**Implementing Real Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now fully embracing the replacement strategy and intend to fully integrate the user\'s scholarship data. I\'m taking extreme care in mapping each data element into the core `Scholarship` structure in `src/types.ts`. I am meticulously mapping the fields, including generating `id` slugs, and formatting the `deadline` strings to match the proper fields. I\'m also addressing `targetDegree` by parsing the eligibility information to simplify this.\n\n\n**Mapping Faculty Eligibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `targetFaculties`, mapping the user\'s \"field_of_study\" to our defined faculties. I am using a strategy of specific keyword lookups and matching to the provided examples. I\'m assigning `[\'All\']` for open fields, and mapping various fields to faculties like `[\'Business/Ivey\']`, `[\'Engineering\']`, and `[\'Law\', \'Social Science\', \'Arts & Humanities\']`. I\'m taking extreme care, so that the fields are consistently assigned correctly. It\'s a key part of how the data will be used.\n\n\n**Refining Data Mappings**\n\nI\'m now refining the data mappings, specifically focusing on `targetFaculties`. I\'ve added mappings for \"Performing Arts\" and \"Music\" to `[\'Music\', \'Arts & Humanities\']`, \"Computer Science\" to `[\'Science\']`, and \"Social Science\" to `[\'Social Science\']`. I am carefully analyzing the data for `minGpaRange`, looking within `eligibility_summary`, `name`, and `notes` to determine academic requirements, and handling various averages such as \'85-89%\' or \'70-74%\'. If unspecified, I\'m setting a default of \'70-74%\'. Lastly, I\'m defining `targetCitizenships` by matching \"Canada\" in `tags` or Canadian citizenship language.\n\n\n**Defining Eligibility Criteria**\n\nI am now focusing on refining various eligibility criteria. I\'m carefully defining `targetCitizenships` based on keywords such as \"international\" or \"Canadian citizen.\" For `targetProvinces`, I\'m looking for \"Ontario\" or Ontario locations. For `requiresFinancialNeed`, I\'m looking for mentions of \"financial need.\" I am also creating logic to define `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests`, based on content or tag keywords.\n\n\n**Defining Interests and Identities**\n\nI\'m now carefully mapping `targetInterests` and `targetIdentities` based on the user\'s data. I am adding \'Leadership\' to `essay_required`, and `STEM research` to `STEM`. I am mapping `arts` to `[\'Arts/music\']` and other open scholarships to `[]`. Now, I am compiling a complete list of all 52 scholarships, taking extreme care to ensure that all values are correct and there are no omissions.\n\n\n**Mapping New Scholarships**\n\nI\'m now integrating new scholarships. I\'ve processed the \"Advertising, Marketing\" and \"AES Engineering\" scholarships. I am defining eligibility, like mapping \"Advertising, Marketing\" to `[\'Business/Ivey\']` and \"AES Engineering\" to `[\'All\']` for the `targetFaculties` field. I am also working on \"Alex & Gillian Davidson Family Endowment\" for Indigenous Students. I am defining `targetCitizenships`, `targetProvinces`, and all other fields.\n\n\n**Defining Further Scholarship Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating more scholarships into the system. I am carefully examining each data point and integrating eligibility requirements. I\'ve defined target criteria, such as \'All\' for provinces and the Canadian citizenship and permanent resident criteria. For instance, in the \"Assignment Saving Lives Program\" and \"Alliance for Equality of Blind Canadians,\" I am implementing target data elements, such as `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests`.\n\n\n**Integrating New Scholarships**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Association of Canadian Universities for Northern Studies,\" the \"Autism Ontario Scholarships,\" and the \"Bank of Canada Scholarship Awards.\" For each, I am accurately mapping fields such as the `deadline`, `targetDegree`, `targetFaculties` (using \'All\' for unspecified fields), and handling `targetCitizenships` and `targetProvinces`, as well as parsing `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests`.\n\n\n**Defining Scholarship Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Barbados Canada Foundation Scholarships.\" I am defining `targetDegree` to be `Undergraduate` and setting the `targetFaculties` to `[\'All\']` for the open field. I\'m also confirming `targetCitizenships` as `Canadian citizen` and `Permanent resident`. I\'ve added a calculated `deadline` for the scholarships. I\'ve also processed the \"Bank of Canada Student Paper Awards\".\n\n\n**Defining Further Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"BeMo Diversity Advocacy Scholarship,\" \"Bill 7 Award for 2SLGBTQI+ Students,\" and \"BBPA National Scholarship Program\". I\'m carefully analyzing the eligibility requirements and mapping them. I am determining key elements, such as `deadline`, `targetDegree`, `targetFaculties`, `targetCitizenships`, and `targetProvinces`, as well as `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests`. In addition, I am determining `requiresFinancialNeed` based on the data provided.\n\n\n\n**Refining Black Scholarship Data**\n\nI am now integrating the \"Black Education Fund\" and the \"Cashion Legal Access to Justice Scholarship.\" I\'m defining deadlines, degrees, and faculties. I am determining target criteria, such as `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests`. I\'m assigning all provinces and Canadian citizenships, mapping \"Law\" and related fields to the proper faculties.\n\n\n**Mapping New Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating new scholarships, specifically the \"Canadian Hearing Services National Scholarship Program\" and the \"Crohn\'s and Colitis Canada Scholarship.\" I am mapping the fields to my existing structure, including `deadline`, `targetDegree`, and `targetFaculties`. I\'ve set the deadline dates, assigned `All` for the faculty, and defined the citizenship requirements. I am carefully handling `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests` based on the provided descriptions.\n\n\n**Defining New Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Dr. Joy Calkin $5000 Student Awards\" and the \"DSLG Student Awards.\" I am mapping the `deadline` to \"April 1, 2027\" and \"June 15, 2026\", respectively. I\'m setting the `targetDegree` to `All` for the first award and `Undergraduate` for the second. The `targetFaculties` will be `All` and `[\'Social Science\', \'Health Sciences\']` respectively. I\'ve also mapped the citizenship requirements, provinces, and interests, handling the financial need flags.\n\n\n**Defining New Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Eaton Indigenous Clean Energy Scholarship,\" \"Greyson Jones Memorial Scholarship,\" and the \"Gunn\'s Hill Wind Farm Renewable Energy Educational Bursary.\" I\'m defining the relevant fields for each. I\'ve mapped the `targetIdentities` and `targetInterests` fields for each, the correct deadlines, and the `targetDegree` to be `All`. I\'m assigning `All` for both citizenship and provinces. I\'ve also parsed the fields to ensure the correct `targetFaculties` field is assigned.\n\n\n\n**Integrating New Scholarships**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Gunn\'s Hill Wind Farm Renewable Energy Educational Bursary,\" the \"Gyan Dhan Scholarship,\" and the \"Hamilton Community Foundation Chaney-Ensign Bursary\". I am defining eligibility details for the Gyan Dhan Scholarship to include STEM research interests. I am assigning the correct deadline dates, setting `targetDegree` to `All`, and mapping fields to ensure the right `targetFaculties`, like `[\'Engineering\', \'Science\']` for the renewable energy field.\n\n\n**Defining Scholarship Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Hamilton Community Foundation Chaney-Ensign Bursary\", \"Hamilton Community Foundation David Davis Memorial Fund\", and the \"Hamilton Community Foundation Geritol Follies Bursary\". I am defining eligibility details for the various scholarships, ensuring that each has been parsed, and the appropriate deadline has been set. I\'m taking care to correctly map each scholarship\'s specific requirements.\n\n\n**Defining Scholarship Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Hellamaid Scholarship Program,\" and the \"Hydro One Awards.\" I am carefully extracting the required values. I\'ve defined the relevant fields, including `deadline`, `targetDegree`, `targetFaculties`, citizenship and provinces. I\'m taking care to correctly assign each field for each scholarship. For \"Hydro One Awards,\" I\'ve included \"Engineering,\" \"Science,\" and \"Business/Ivey\" for the faculties, matching with the provided data.\n\n\n\n**Defining Further Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Indspire\" and \"James Kreppner Memorial Scholarship and Bursary Program\". For the Indspire scholarship, I\'m assigning the deadline, and making it \"November 1, 2026.\" I am setting the degree to `All`, and defining the location criteria to \'All\' for provinces, and \'Canadian citizen\' and \'Permanent resident\' for citizenships. For the \"James Kreppner Memorial Scholarship and Bursary Program\", I will set the relevant fields, including setting it to \'All\'. I am setting the \"Longhouse Business Award\" to \"August 31, 2026\".\n\n\n**Defining Loran & Lumine Criteria**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Loran Award, mapping its fields according to the provided data. I am setting the deadline to \"October 15, 2026,\" and setting the relevant degree and faculty fields. I\'m mapping citizenship and province, and including the relevant interests. Next, I am working on the Lumine Future Leaders in Technology & Business Scholarship, carefully assigning deadlines, and setting the relevant fields and faculties. I am also mapping to the correct location criteria.\n\n\n**Defining MADD and Manulife**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"MADD Canada\" scholarship, setting the deadline to \"May 31, 2026\", and the degree to \"All\" (Undergraduate, Graduate). I\'ve set faculties to \'All\', and defined locations as Canadian citizens and all provinces. I\'m also including \'Leadership\' for the interests. Then, I\'m integrating the \"Manulife Life Lessons\" scholarship, setting the deadline to \"March 31, 2027\", and degree as `Undergraduate`. Both citizenships will be Canadian citizens and permanent residents, with all provinces.\n\n\n**Mapping New Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"McCall MacBain Scholarships\" and \"TD Scholarship in Computer Science\". For the McCall scholarship, I am assigning the deadline to \"September 30, 2026,\" setting the degree to `Graduate`, and faculties to `All`. I am also assigning citizenship as Canadian, and permanent resident. The `targetInterests` include \'Leadership\' and \'Volunteering\'. For the TD Scholarship, I am including \"September 30, 2026,\" as the deadline date and setting `targetDegree` to `Undergraduate`. The target faculties for this scholarship are `[\'Science\']`.\n\n\n**Integrating Final Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"TD Scholarship in Engineering\" and \"TD Scholarship in Information and Media Studies\". I am adding each scholarship and accurately defining all criteria. For the TD Engineering scholarship, I have set the deadline to \"September 30, 2026\", and the degree to `Undergraduate`. Its `targetFaculties` field is `[\'Engineering\']`, and it requires Canadian citizens or permanent residents with financial need in Ontario. For the TD in Media Studies, I am setting all relevant data fields.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Scholarship Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final scholarships: \"Betty Schecter Memorial Scholarship\" and \"Chris Binns-Smith Memorial Scholarship\". I\'ve assigned deadlines and degree levels to both. I\'ve set the target faculties, including Computer Science to `[\'Science\']`. I\'m integrating location data, setting the minimum GPA, determining financial need and the relevant interests. Finally, I\'m integrating the identities and completing all necessary fields for the integration.\n\n\n**Defining Final Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Spadotto and Greco Family Women in Engineering Award\" and the \"John Schecter Memorial Scholarship in Computer Science\". I have mapped the relevant fields, with accurate deadlines, and including the relevant data. For the Schecter award, the deadline is September 30, 2026, with Undergraduate degree and Science faculty, and the location criteria. I am also mapping the GPA and interests and integrating the information into the overall data.\n\n\n**Integrating Final Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the remaining scholarships. I\'ve mapped the \"James Emerson Miles Admission Scholarship,\" defining `Undergraduate` for degree, `[\'Engineering\']` for faculty, and Ontario for the location. I\'ve set financial need to `true` and the GPA range. Lastly, I\'m integrating the \"Ivey Foundation Awards for International Exchange,\" with careful attention to all fields.\n\n\n**Finalizing Scholarship Integration**\n\nI am now integrating the final scholarships. These are the \"Dean\'s Undergraduate Scholarship in Social Science,\" and the \"Mary Louise and Dr. Peter Cameron Scholarships.\" I have mapped deadlines, degree, and faculty information for both, meticulously ensuring accuracy for all fields, particularly the location, financial need, and interests for each. I\'m carefully compiling and reviewing all the scholarships.\n\n\n**Mapping Western\'s Scholarship Data**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the Western University scholarships, specifically the \"Western Continuing Admission Scholarship of Excellence\" for Black students and students with disabilities. I\'m mapping the deadlines, degree levels, and locations accurately for both. I am defining financial need and interests. I\'m assigning the relevant faculties for the open fields.\n\n\n**Integrating Western University Scholarships**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Western Continuing Admission Scholarship of Excellence for Indigenous Students\" and the \"Neen Hodgins Indigenous Continuing Admission Scholarship.\" I am meticulously assigning deadlines, degree levels, locations, identities, and interests for both. I\'ve set the minimum GPA ranges for each and also specified faculties and financial need. I\'m focusing on ensuring data accuracy for both scholarships.\n\n\n**Finalizing Scholarship Data Integration**\n\nI am now integrating the final scholarships: \"Jack Andrew Kwan International Award in Engineering\" and \"Dennis Logan Award\". I am setting all fields for the new scholarships. For the \"Kwan\" award, the deadline is set to September 30, 2026, the degree is `Undergraduate`, and the location is Ontario for international students. The \"Dennis Logan Award\" is also set to the deadline September 30, 2026, is open to all degree types, and requires Ontario residents.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
